{"name":"Youthful Coral","hex":"#ee8073","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"youthful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Young or seeming young.","Characteristic of young people."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/youthful"},{"term":"coral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of many species of marine invertebrates in the class Anthozoa, most of which build hard calcium carbonate skeletons and form colonies, or a colony belonging to one of those species.","A hard substance made of the skeletons of these organisms."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of coral.","Having the orange-pink color of coral."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coral"}],"entries":[{"title":"Youthful","blocks":[{"text":"\"Youthful\" is a song by New Zealand singer and television presenter Anika Moa, released as her debut single and as the lead single from her first studio album, Thinking Room (2001). Moa wrote the song before she joined Atlantic Records and recorded Thinking Room, which was produced by Victor Van Vugt. Although the song was released commercially in Australia and was serviced to US radio in early 2002, it was never issued as a single in New Zealand. Despite this, it received plentiful airplay in the country, allowing it to reach number five on the RIANZ Singles Chart in October 2001. At the 2002 New Zealand Music Awards, \"Youthful\" won Moa the award for Best Songwriter."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0c/Youthful_Anika_Moa_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Youthful","wikidata":"Q116291134"},{"title":"Coral","blocks":[{"text":"Corals are colonial marine invertebrates within the subphylum Anthozoa of the phylum Cnidaria. They typically form compact colonies of many identical individual polyps. Coral species include the important reef builders that inhabit tropical oceans and 